1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,089
A dark kitchen at night.

2
00:00:02,089 --> 00:00:03,391
A light flicks on.

3
00:00:03,391 --> 00:00:05,602
A cockroach dashes under the shelf.

4
00:00:06,002 --> 00:00:08,742
Gone in a second, before
anyone could move.

5
00:00:09,192 --> 00:00:10,500
Aarav saw it happen.

6
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,992
He asked: how did it sense him so fast?

7
00:00:12,992 --> 00:00:15,941
And how does a body with
no bones keep its shape?

8
00:00:16,291 --> 00:00:17,860
Two features answer that.

9
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:20,132
A hard outer skeleton made of chitin.

10
00:00:20,132 --> 00:00:23,333
And sense organs and nerves
spread all along its body.

11
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:27,778
By the end, you will know the
cockroach's body, mouth parts and wings,

12
00:00:27,778 --> 00:00:31,869
and its digestion, blood, breathing,
excretion, nerves and life cycle.

13
00:00:32,519 --> 00:00:34,884
First, meet the cockroach,
Periplaneta americana.

14
00:00:35,234 --> 00:00:38,658
It is brown or black, about
34 to 53 millimetres long.

15
00:00:38,658 --> 00:00:43,023
It is active at night, eats almost
anything, and lives in damp places.

16
00:00:43,473 --> 00:00:46,491
Its body has three parts:
head, thorax and abdomen.

17
00:00:46,491 --> 00:00:50,386
A hard exoskeleton of chitin covers
it, made of plates called sclerites,

18
00:00:50,386 --> 00:00:52,823
joined by thin, bendy
arthrodial membranes.

19
00:00:53,473 --> 00:00:55,305
Let's zoom into the cockroach.

20
00:00:55,655 --> 00:01:00,410
The thorax has three parts:
prothorax, mesothorax and metathorax.

21
00:01:00,410 --> 00:01:03,359
Each one bears a pair of walking legs.

22
00:01:03,859 --> 00:01:05,203
Zoom to the head.

23
00:01:05,203 --> 00:01:10,008
It is triangular, made of six fused
segments, with a pair of compound eyes

24
00:01:10,008 --> 00:01:14,010
and two long, thread-like antennae
that sense the surroundings.

25
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:17,272
Now the mouth parts, made
for biting and chewing.

26
00:01:17,272 --> 00:01:18,844
An upper lip, the labrum.

27
00:01:18,844 --> 00:01:21,275
A pair of mandibles
and a pair of maxillae.

28
00:01:21,275 --> 00:01:23,021
And a lower lip, the labium.

29
00:01:23,521 --> 00:01:26,565
In the middle sits the hypopharynx,
which works like a tongue.

30
00:01:27,215 --> 00:01:30,269
Now its wings and abdomen, step by step.

31
00:01:30,619 --> 00:01:31,519
Step one.

32
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:34,447
The first pair of wings
grows from the mesothorax.

33
00:01:34,447 --> 00:01:38,116
These forewings are the tegmina:
dark, leathery and opaque.

34
00:01:38,116 --> 00:01:40,323
They cover the hind wings at rest.

35
00:01:41,073 --> 00:01:41,973
Step two.

36
00:01:41,842 --> 00:01:44,441
The second pair grows from the metathorax.

37
00:01:44,441 --> 00:01:48,194
These hind wings are thin,
see-through, and used for flying.

38
00:01:48,944 --> 00:01:49,844
Step three.

39
00:01:49,759 --> 00:01:53,081
The abdomen has ten segments,
in both males and females.

40
00:01:53,831 --> 00:01:54,731
Step four.

41
00:01:54,606 --> 00:01:58,860
In females, the seventh, eighth and
ninth sterna, the plates on the belly

42
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:01,646
side, form a brood
pouch, the genital pouch.

43
00:02:02,396 --> 00:02:03,296
Step five.

44
00:02:03,231 --> 00:02:07,388
Both sexes have a pair of jointed
anal cerci on the tenth segment.

45
00:02:07,388 --> 00:02:10,334
Only males have short,
thread-like anal styles.

46
00:02:11,084 --> 00:02:12,053
Remember this.

47
00:02:12,053 --> 00:02:13,438
Forewings are tegmina.

48
00:02:13,438 --> 00:02:14,506
Hind wings fly.

49
00:02:15,106 --> 00:02:16,006
Now inside.

50
00:02:15,924 --> 00:02:17,923
Follow food through the cockroach.

51
00:02:18,273 --> 00:02:22,616
From the mouth, food passes the
pharynx and oesophagus into the crop, a

52
00:02:22,616 --> 00:02:24,076
sac that stores food.

53
00:02:24,526 --> 00:02:25,926
Next is the gizzard.

54
00:02:25,926 --> 00:02:30,219
Inside it are six hard, chitinous
plates, called teeth, that grind the

55
00:02:30,219 --> 00:02:31,119
food.

56
00:02:31,195 --> 00:02:35,522
Where the foregut meets the midgut, six
to eight hepatic caeca make digestive

57
00:02:35,522 --> 00:02:36,422
juice.

58
00:02:36,074 --> 00:02:40,346
Where the midgut meets the hindgut,
thin Malpighian tubules join the gut.

59
00:02:40,996 --> 00:02:44,976
A cockroach breathes and moves its
blood very differently from us.

60
00:02:45,326 --> 00:02:48,510
It breathes through a network
of tubes called tracheae.

61
00:02:48,510 --> 00:02:52,719
They open outside through ten pairs
of small holes, the spiracles, on the

62
00:02:52,719 --> 00:02:53,969
sides of the body.

63
00:02:53,969 --> 00:02:56,047
Air travels straight to the cells.

64
00:02:56,496 --> 00:02:58,033
Its blood system is open.

65
00:02:58,033 --> 00:03:01,192
The few blood vessels open
into a space, the haemocoel.

66
00:03:01,192 --> 00:03:03,762
The blood, called
haemolymph, is colourless.

67
00:03:04,212 --> 00:03:07,009
A long, tube-shaped heart
runs along the back.

68
00:03:07,009 --> 00:03:10,551
Its chambers have tiny openings,
the ostia, on each side.

69
00:03:11,201 --> 00:03:13,571
Waste is removed by
the Malpighian tubules.

70
00:03:13,571 --> 00:03:16,589
The cockroach excretes uric
acid, so it is uricotelic.

71
00:03:16,939 --> 00:03:21,509
Its nervous system is a chain of ganglia,
small knots of nerve cells, along

72
00:03:21,509 --> 00:03:22,623
the belly side.

73
00:03:22,623 --> 00:03:25,644
Three are in the thorax
and six in the abdomen.

74
00:03:25,644 --> 00:03:29,128
In the head, the brain is the
supra-oesophageal ganglion.

75
00:03:29,578 --> 00:03:33,827
Because nerves run all along the body,
a headless cockroach can live for

76
00:03:33,827 --> 00:03:34,896
up to a week.

77
00:03:34,896 --> 00:03:39,228
And each compound eye has about two
thousand units, the ommatidia, giving

78
00:03:39,228 --> 00:03:40,232
mosaic vision.

79
00:03:40,832 --> 00:03:41,732
Your turn.

80
00:03:41,487 --> 00:03:45,042
Which removes waste from a cockroach's
blood: the gizzard, or the Malpighian

81
00:03:45,042 --> 00:03:45,942
tubules?

82
00:03:45,576 --> 00:03:46,540
Pause and decide.

83
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:51,000
The Malpighian tubules!

84
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,596
The gizzard only grinds food.

85
00:03:53,246 --> 00:03:54,968
Now, a worked example.

86
00:03:54,968 --> 00:03:58,066
The life of a cockroach,
from egg to adult.

87
00:03:58,416 --> 00:03:59,714
The sexes are separate.

88
00:03:59,714 --> 00:04:01,305
Males have a pair of testes.

89
00:04:01,305 --> 00:04:04,805
Females have a pair of large ovaries,
each made of eight ovarioles.

90
00:04:05,255 --> 00:04:09,378
Fertilised eggs are packed in a
dark brown capsule, the ootheca.

91
00:04:09,378 --> 00:04:14,011
A female makes nine to ten oothecae,
each with fourteen to sixteen eggs.

92
00:04:14,461 --> 00:04:15,605
A nymph hatches.

93
00:04:15,605 --> 00:04:19,775
It looks like a small adult without
wings, and it moults about thirteen

94
00:04:19,775 --> 00:04:20,675
times.

95
00:04:20,793 --> 00:04:22,237
Only the adult has wings.

96
00:04:22,237 --> 00:04:25,719
Growing through nymphs like this is
called paurometabolous development.

97
00:04:26,369 --> 00:04:27,831
Now, the exam trap.

98
00:04:28,181 --> 00:04:32,102
Many students think a cockroach's
blood flows in closed tubes, like ours.

99
00:04:32,502 --> 00:04:33,735
But its system is open.

100
00:04:33,735 --> 00:04:36,781
Haemolymph flows into the haemocoel
and bathes the organs directly.

101
00:04:37,431 --> 00:04:38,688
Where is this asked?

102
00:04:38,688 --> 00:04:42,537
As statement or match questions on
mouth parts, wings, Malpighian tubules

103
00:04:42,537 --> 00:04:43,575
and the ootheca.

104
00:04:44,175 --> 00:04:45,341
Exam level now.

105
00:04:45,341 --> 00:04:47,376
Match each part with its job.

106
00:04:47,376 --> 00:04:48,591
Pause and solve.

107
00:04:53,991 --> 00:04:55,346
The answer is A.

108
00:04:55,346 --> 00:04:57,541
One-q, two-p, three-s, four-r.

109
00:04:58,041 --> 00:04:59,576
Tegmina are the forewings.

110
00:04:59,576 --> 00:05:01,025
The gizzard grinds food.

111
00:05:01,525 --> 00:05:03,516
Malpighian tubules remove waste.

112
00:05:03,516 --> 00:05:05,820
And the ootheca is the egg capsule.

113
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:07,960
Here is your recap.

114
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,543
Screenshot this card.

115
00:05:12,743 --> 00:05:14,929
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

116
00:05:15,329 --> 00:05:16,229
One.

117
00:05:15,741 --> 00:05:18,402
How many pairs of spiracles
does a cockroach have?

118
00:05:19,302 --> 00:05:20,202
Two.

119
00:05:19,707 --> 00:05:21,137
What does the gizzard do?

120
00:05:22,037 --> 00:05:22,937
Three.

121
00:05:22,567 --> 00:05:23,817
What is an ootheca?

122
00:05:24,917 --> 00:05:29,235
Next time: a frog, a cockroach and you
are all built from tiny living units.

123
00:05:29,235 --> 00:05:30,182
What are they?

124
00:05:30,182 --> 00:05:32,521
We find out in cell, the unit of life.
